What is a Wheel Speed Sensor?
A wheel speed sensor is a vital electronic component that provides real-time data to a vehicle's onboard computer. This information is essential for the proper operation of safety-critical systems including Anti-lock Braking Systems (ABS) and Electronic Stability Control (ESC). These systems rely on precise wheel speed inputs to prevent wheel lock-up during braking, enhance vehicle stability during cornering, and manage traction in slippery conditions.
